##SALES AND REVENUE TRACKING
Once you start publishing content and promoting your ebook, the next step is to monitor sales and track your performance. This helps you understand which marketing strategies are working and how much profit your ebook business is generating.



Monitor Your Gumroad Sales -
Open your Gumroad dashboard.
Navigate to the Sales or Analytics section.
Check the number of ebook purchases.
Monitor your total revenue and available balance.
Review individual transactions and refund requests.
Keep track of your payout status.



Track Your Threads Performance -
Monitor how your posts are performing and identify which content attracts potential buyers.

Track metrics such as: 
Views and impressions.
Likes and replies.
Reposts and shares.
Profile visits.
Link clicks.
Follower growth.



Identify Your Best-Performing Content - 
Review your top-performing Threads posts.
Identify which topics and hooks attract the most engagement.
Check which posts generate profile visits and product link clicks.
Compare promotional posts with value-based posts.
Create more content around topics that attract relevant potential customers.



Calculate Your Actual Profit - 

Track the following:
Total ebook sales.
Gross revenue.
Gumroad and payment processing fees.
Refunds and other expenses.
Advertising and software costs.
Net profit.


Example:
Particulars                Amount
20 ebook sales × $10       $200
Platform and payment fees  $25
Other expenses             $15
Net profit                 $160



Maintain a Sales Tracker - 
Use Google Sheets to record your daily and monthly performance.

Suggested columns:
Date
Threads posts published
Post views
Profile visits
Product link clicks
Ebook sales
Revenue
Expenses
Net profit



Things to Keep in Mind - 
Review your sales and analytics regularly.
Don't judge your strategy solely by post views.
Focus on link clicks and actual purchases.
Identify which content generates paying customers.
Keep records of refunds, fees and expenses.
Use your findings to improve your marketing strategy.



Useful tools - 
Gumroad Dashboard – Sales and revenue tracking.
Threads Insights – Available post and account performance data.
Google Sheets – Sales, expenses and profit tracking.
